---
import { ShieldCheck } from "@lucide/astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sift benchmark methodology"
  description="Read how Sift separates development data, blinded holdout evaluation, human review, deployed-path checks, and public reliability claims."
  path="/reliability/methodology"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Benchmark method"
    title="Measure each failure mode without turning it into a safety promise."
    description="Sift's benchmark is designed to test menu reading, evidence handling, conservative risk labels, uncertainty, staff questions, translation, stability, and deployed behavior as separate responsibilities."
    compact
  />

  <section class="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
    <div class="shell status__inner">
      <ShieldCheck size={34} stroke-width={1.6} aria-hidden="true" />
      <div>
        <h2 id="status-title">Current status: methodology ready, performance gate open.</h2>
        <p>
          The repository has a 60-case development set and a separate 48-case / 24-group synthetic candidate. Twelve
          cases test a menu language that differs from the user's language. The candidate cannot freeze until exactly
          12 cases across six groups are replaced with reviewed real-world menus and an external perceptual plus visual
          duplicate audit is approved. Six possible source pages have been researched, visually screened as menu
          candidates, and bound to stricter source-intake rules. A completed current-version download receipt,
          independent rights, suitability, transformation, labels, and duplicate audit remain pending, so they are not
          yet holdout evidence. Model
          experiments have not run, and the candidate has zero model-produced benchmark results. No reliability
          percentage or launch-readiness claim is available.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="methodology">
    <section class="shell section" aria-labelledby="roles-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p>01 / Data roles</p>
        <h2 id="roles-title">Development work and final evidence stay separate.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__body">
        <dl class="data-roles">
          <div>
            <dt>Development</dt>
            <dd>60 cases in 23 menu groups for prompt, policy, ontology, validator, scorer, and regression work.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Candidate holdout</dt>
            <dd>48 synthetic cases in 24 non-overlapping groups. Promotion requires exactly 12 reviewed real-world cases with source and review lineage across six groups.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Deployed canaries</dt>
            <dd>A fixed 12-case multilingual clear/poor set for authentication, fallback, telemetry, validation, and latency.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p>
          Development results can reveal failures, but they cannot estimate unseen performance. Holdout results become
          reportable only after label approval, lineage-verified freezing, and one locked run. Canaries verify the
          deployed path; they do not replace the model-quality holdout.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="protocol" aria-labelledby="protocol-title">
      <div class="shell section">
        <div class="section__heading">
          <p>02 / Protocol</p>
          <h2 id="protocol-title">Configuration drift starts a new run.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section__body">
          <ol>
            <li>Freeze model, thinking level, image preparation, prompt order, prompt, schemas, ontology, policy, validators, and scorer.</li>
            <li>Hash the exact configuration, benchmark manifest, prepared image bytes, and a separate scoring manifest bound to labels and grouping.</li>
            <li>Use a fresh model session for every case and repeat without exposing expected labels.</li>
            <li>Make one provider call, validate raw structured output, preserve observed evidence, then apply server normalization and deterministic risk policy.</li>
            <li>Run the actual client validator before scoring any user-visible result.</li>
            <li>Preserve every fallback, timeout, malformed output, exclusion, and missing metric in its denominator.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="shell section" aria-labelledby="review-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p>03 / Human review</p>
        <h2 id="review-title">Structured output still needs human judgment.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__body">
        <p>
          Reviewers inspect the exact image bytes and label visible evidence, plausible patterns, unknown information,
          accepted risk ranges, benign controls, and required question intent. Critical holdout cases require an
          independent second reviewer.
        </p>
        <p>
          A separate blinded review checks whether visible-text claims are supported by the image and whether
          restaurant-language messages and questions remain faithful to the user's language. Automated lexical checks
          cannot establish translation quality. Any unsupported visible claim, material translation error, missed
          question intent, unreviewable required item, or missing expected item blocks release. The combined report
          re-scores the filled template against its sealed key and verifies its run, configuration, requirements,
          manifest, and frozen lineage rather than trusting a stored pass flag.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="metrics" aria-labelledby="metrics-title">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="metrics__heading">
          <p>04 / Release gates</p>
          <h2 id="metrics-title">Report safety-critical failures before averages.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Sift private beta reliability gates">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Measure</th><th scope="col">Private-beta gate</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Direct severe-allergen misses</th><td>0</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Deterministic under-escalations</th><td>0</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Unsupported assurance claims</th><td>0</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Invalid client-visible results</th><td>0</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Poor-image retake behavior</th><td>100%</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Unsupported visible-text claims</th><td>0 after human review</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Material translation errors</th><td>0, with no required item unreviewable</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Required staff-question coverage</th><td>100% after human review</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Clear or partial successful-result rate</th><td>At least 95%</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Benign high or avoid rate</th><td>At most 10%</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Critical repeat drift</th><td>0 label flips or non-ordinal comparisons; exact dish/readability agreement</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Required language slices</th><td>Every slice passes its safety gates</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Deployed canary</th><td>Fixed 12-case set passes with telemetry verified</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Deployed latency</th><td>p95 at most 15s; p99 at most 25s</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="metrics__note">
          These are acceptance thresholds, not measured results. Every rate must publish its numerator, denominator,
          confidence interval where applicable, case scope, exclusions, configuration identity, and known failures.
          The failure-registry snapshot for this documentation pass has 46 entries, with 43 resolved and three open:
          provider access, the missing real-world holdout subset plus human and duplicate review, and unmeasured live multi-page
          completeness. That status is not a model
          reliability percentage. Combined reporting recomputes raw phase evidence, canary telemetry, and human review;
          every live release phase remains pending.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="shell section" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p>05 / Limits</p>
        <h2 id="limits-title">A menu benchmark cannot observe a kitchen.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__body">
        <ul>
          <li>Menu images cannot verify complete recipes, substitutions, suppliers, or cross-contact controls.</li>
          <li>The candidate is synthetic-only and cannot freeze until its 12-case real-world subset and duplicate audit exist.</li>
          <li>Small language, cuisine, allergen, severity, and image-quality slices require exact denominators.</li>
          <li>Runtime and evaluation tooling accept up to four ordered pages; the 8-case diagnostic still has no model responses.</li>
          <li>Model and provider behavior can change, so the same tests must be repeated after material changes.</li>
          <li>No benchmark result makes a dish safe or replaces confirmation with restaurant staff.</li>
        </ul>
        <nav aria-label="Related information">
          <a href="/reliability">Reliability overview <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
          <a href="/safety">Safety boundary <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .status {
    background: var(--teal-100);
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 72px);
  }

  .status__inner {
    align-items: start;
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  .status svg {
    color: var(--teal-700);
    margin-top: 5px;
  }

  .status h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.55rem);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .status p {
    color: #29433f;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  .methodology {
    background: var(--cream);
  }

  .section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 38px clamp(56px, 10vw, 150px);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr);
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 122px);
  }

  .section__heading > p,
  .metrics__heading > p {
    color: var(--teal-700);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .section__heading h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section__body {
    color: #34433f;
    max-width: 74ch;
  }

  .section__body p:last-child,
  .section__body ul:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .data-roles {
    margin: 0 0 36px;
  }

  .data-roles div {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 0.45fr) minmax(0, 1.55fr);
    padding-block: 18px;
  }

  .data-roles div:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .data-roles dt {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .data-roles dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .protocol {
    background: var(--teal-900);
    color: var(--white);
  }

  .protocol h2 {
    color: var(--white);
  }

  .protocol .section__heading > p {
    color: var(--tangerine);
  }

  .protocol .section__body {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.84);
  }

  .protocol ol {
    counter-reset: protocol;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .protocol li {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
    counter-increment: protocol;
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
    grid-template-columns: 32px minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: 18px;
  }

  .protocol li::before {
    color: var(--tangerine);
    content: counter(protocol, decimal-leading-zero);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    padding-top: 3px;
  }

  .protocol li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
  }

  .metrics {
    background: var(--warm);
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 122px);
  }

  .metrics__heading {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 44px;
  }

  .metrics__heading h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .table-wrap:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--teal-600);
    outline-offset: 6px;
  }

  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    min-width: 680px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  th,
  td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 17px 24px 18px 0;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  thead th {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  tbody th {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    width: 62%;
  }

  .metrics__note {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    max-width: 82ch;
  }

  .section__body li {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .section__body nav {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: grid;
    margin-top: 36px;
  }

  .section__body a {
    align-items: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--teal-700);
    display: flex;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    justify-content: space-between;
    min-height: 52px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .status__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .data-roles div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
